Subject: [PATCH 4/4] fix(security): Phase G findings from the real Claude Code
 staging run

1. False positive (V2.1 regression): a worker wrote a test file through a data
   heredoc whose body contained `import ... from '../src/slugify.ts'`. The path
   check tokenized the body, resolved ../src to <agent home>/workspaces/src and
   denied the call. Heredoc bodies are now removed before the path-resolution
   check, but ONLY when the shell analyzer classifies them as data. Heredocs fed
   to an interpreter, unquoted bodies with substitutions and heredoc-written files
   executed in the same command keep the raw text. The literal agent-path check
   still sees bodies. Replay of the real transcript: the denied call is now allowed.
2. Usage accounting: the key-name redaction rule matched "token" and stored every
   execution's inputTokens/outputTokens as [REDACTED]. Numbers and booleans are no
   longer redacted by key name; string values still are.

69 probes: 0 bypasses, 0 legitimate regressions. Rule K matrix: 0 FN, 4 FP (unchanged).
